.TH CLEAR 1.SH NAMEclear \- clear the screen.SH SYNOPSIS\fBclear\fR.SH DESCRIPTION\fBclear\fRclears the terminal's screen, with the escape sequence it reads from thetermcap entry for\fBTERM\fR.\fRIt takes no options.\fBcls\fRdoes the same job; either will do..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOcls, tput